  "answer": "I'll start by reading the debugging skill, then trace why special prices with an end date never appear on the storefront.The storefront price check treats a future end date as if it were still in the future after the start has already passed, and product create writes the end date into the start-date field. I'll add a failing test for that, then fix both.Special prices with an end date were dropped in two places. Creating a product stored the end date in the special start-date field, and the storefront price calculation then required that same start date to be after today, which can never be true once the special has begun. The end date is now saved on the end-date field, and a special applies when the start date is already past and the end date is still ahead.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core -am test -Dtest=ProductSpecialPriceTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\", \"mvn -pl sm-shop -am test -Dtest=PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\", \"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am test -Dtest=ProductSpecialPriceTest,PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"live admin and storefront REST calls\", \"products already saved with the end date written into the start-date column\"], \"missing\": [\"an integration fixture that creates a product through the admin API and reads it from the storefront\"]}",
